pve-wedge-watchdog (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Upgrades no longer leave the watchdog stopped: --no-stop-on-upgrade plus
    a restart in postinst when the unit is enabled (0.1.0 -> 0.1.1
    silently disarmed it).
  * Move StartLimitIntervalSec to [Unit], where systemd reads it.

 -- Danya Generalov <danya@danya02.ru>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 11:54:41 +0300

pve-wedge-watchdog (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the passthrough memory guard hookscript in
    /usr/share/pve-wedge-watchdog/ and guard hugepages VMs too.
  * Per-VM bypass: PVE_GUARD_SKIP and /etc/pve-passthrough-guard.d/<vmid>.skip,
    logged to the task log.
  * New pve-passthrough-guard-sync service + 5-minute timer (enabled) that
    deploys the snippet and attaches it to unhooked pinned-memory VMs.

 -- Danya Generalov <danya@danya02.ru>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 08:47:00 +0000

